    "description": "Ethiopian Women with Disabilities National Association Vacancy Announcement Ethiopian Women with Disability National Association (EWDNA) is a local, nonprofit making, nongovernmental organization based in Addis Ababa with 11 branches in Amhara (Gonder, Bahir Dar, Mehale Meda), Oromia (Ambo, jimma, Adama) SNNPR (Arba Minch) Sidama region Hawassa city and Sheger city Sebeta town and Dire Dawa. EWDNA is established in September 2002 with the initiation and struggle of 7 women with disabilities and one non-disabled woman. EWDNA works on women with 5 types of disabilities; women with visual, hearing, physical & intellectual disability, and women affected by leprosy. EWDNA has 12,590 members of girls and women with disabilities across the country. Position: SRH Project officer Report to: SRH alliance Project Coordinator Required number: 1 Salary: As per the organizations Salary Scale Place of Work: Amhra region; Sekota town and Sekota Zuriya Woreda Duration of Employment: one year with possibility of extension based on performance and availability of fund. Job Summary: The Project Officer is responsible for the day-to-day implementation, monitoring, and reporting of SRH project activities in line with the Association quality standards, donor compliance requirements, and safeguarding policies. The role ensures that project interventions effectively address the needs of Women with disabilities, youth, adolescents, and vulnerable communities, with a strong focus on gender equality, inclusion, and protection. This is a full-time, project-dedicated role at 100% Level of Effort. Key Responsibilities: Implement approved project activities in accordance with the Detailed Implementation Plan (DIP) and log-frame. Ensure activities are gender and disability and youth-responsive, and inclusive, and, in line with organizations, Plan International’s Global Strategy and donor standards. Provide technical support during community mobilization, training, awareness-raising, and service delivery activities. Collect accurate, timely, and quality data using EWDNA tools and systems. Support routine monitoring, beneficiary feedback mechanisms, and learning documentation. Contribute to donor and internal reports (weekly, monthly, quarterly, biannual and annual Work closely with local government offices specially; health office, education offices community structures, and other implementing partners. Support coordination meetings and lead the advocacy campaigns at woreda and kebele levels. Properly engage government stakeholders and service providers specially health institutions/facilities youths, women and OPD associations at each project activities /process. Provide guidance, coaching, and appropriate technical support to the community structures, youth and OPDs and volunteers. Ensure full compliance with EWDNAs Safeguarding Policy and Code of Conduct and other policies and procedures. Coordinate disability- and youth-focused awareness-raising and community dialogue sessions, addressing stigma, gender equality, harmful practices, teenage pregnancy, and child marriage. Promote safe programming and accountability to affected populations. Frequent travel to the project location at targeted kebele including hard to reach kebeles .",
