    "description": "ST GEORGE’S SCHOOL VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT – HEAD OF SECURITY Location: Gondar, Ethiopia Position: Head of Security Reports to: Executive Director Job Purpose St George’s School is seeking a highly experienced, disciplined and dependable Head of Security to take overall responsibility for the safety and security of the school, its students, staff, visitors and property. The successful candidate will provide strong leadership to the security team, ensure that all guards perform their duties effectively and introduce and maintain security measures to prevent theft, burglary, unauthorized access and any form of security threat. The Head of Security will be expected to maintain a high level of vigilance at all times and respond promptly to any security incident or potential threat. Key Responsibilities A. Management and Supervision of Security Guards Supervise and manage all security guards to ensure that they are present, alert, disciplined and performing their duties effectively at all times. Prepare and maintain an effective guard duty timetable, making proper use of available security personnel and ensuring that all areas of the school are adequately covered. Conduct regular and random inspections to confirm that guards are carrying out their assigned duties. Assess the competence, discipline and performance of all guards. Arrange for the replacement of any guard who is incompetent, unreliable, careless or unsuitable for the role with a competent and dependable replacement. Ensure that guards understand and follow school security procedures. B. Protection of School Property Take all necessary measures to ensure that school buildings, equipment, furniture, vehicles, stores and other property are protected against theft, burglary, vandalism and attack. Identify security weaknesses around the school compound and recommend appropriate improvements. Introduce and oversee effective security measures, including window bars, security cameras, adequate lighting, secure gates, locks and other necessary protective systems. Regularly inspect the school compound to identify possible security risks and ensure that they are addressed promptly. Ensure that all school property remains properly protected, including during evenings, weekends and school holidays. C. Access Control and Movement Records Ensure that no person enters the school compound without proper authorization. Ensure that all visitors are identified, authorized and recorded before being allowed to enter the premises. Maintain proper records of staff and students entering or leaving the school compound outside normal authorized hours. Ensure that any staff member entering or leaving the school at an unusual time has the necessary authorization and that the Finance and Administration Manager is informed. Coordinate with the Registrar to verify that any student entering or leaving the school at an unusual time has been properly authorized and recorded. Pay particular attention to staff members and students who repeatedly enter or leave the school at irregular times and report any concerning patterns to the Executive Director. Ensure that guards do not allow students or staff to leave the school compound without following the school's established procedures. D. Prevention of Theft and Unauthorized Removal of Property Establish and supervise appropriate measures to prevent school property from being removed without authorization. Oversee random and reasonable checks of staff bags and personal belongings as they leave the school compound, in accordance with school policy and applicable law. Ensure that such checks are conducted respectfully, consistently and without discrimination. Ensure that any suspected theft or unauthorized removal of school property is reported immediately to the Executive Director. Maintain proper records of security incidents, suspected losses and actions taken. E. Firearms and Security Equipment Take responsibility for identifying the need for firearms where legally and operationally necessary. Prepare and submit requests for the acquisition of firearms and the necessary licenses or permits through the appropriate legal and government authorities. Ensure that no firearm is acquired, carried, stored or used without the required legal authorization. Ensure that any authorized firearms are handled, stored and controlled safely and responsibly, in accordance with Ethiopian law. Identify other security equipment required for the effective operation of the security team and submit requests for approval. F. Security Incidents and Reporting Immediately inform the School Management and Executive Director of any security breach, attempted break-in, theft, attack, suspicious activity or other potential threat. Request additional security personnel, equipment or other support whenever necessary. Investigate security concerns within the limits of the position's authority and report findings to the School Management and the Executive Director. Maintain a written record of all significant security incidents and the action taken. Submit a monthly security report to the School Management and the Executive Director covering: Security incidents and attempted breaches. Attendance and performance of security guards. Unusual movements of staff and students. Suspected thefts or losses of school property. Security weaknesses identified and improvements made. Additional security needs and recommendations. G. Child Safeguarding and Enforcement of School Rules The Head of Security will be expected to act as the school's principal security and safeguarding contact, helping to ensure that all children are safe and protected at all times, including outside normal school working hours. The responsibilities will include: Protection of children: Ensure that no child is threatened, physically abused, intimidated, bullied or mistreated by any member of staff, student, visitor or other person on the school premises. First point of contact: Serve as the first point of contact for reporting cases or allegations of physical abuse, threats, intimidation or mistreatment of children. All such incidents must be taken seriously, reported immediately to the Executive Director and handled in accordance with the school's child safeguarding procedures. Zero tolerance for corporal punishment: Ensure that corporal punishment is strictly prohibited throughout the school premises and that no person uses physical punishment against any child under any circumstances. Safeguarding outside normal working hours: Maintain appropriate security and supervision arrangements to protect children during evenings, weekends, holidays and other periods outside normal school working hours. Enforcement of school rules: Help ensure that all school rules and regulations are respected and upheld at all times by staff, students, visitors and other persons on the premises. Prohibited activities: Ensure that smoking, drinking alcohol, possessing or using illegal drugs or other prohibited substances, and any other unlawful or prohibited activities are not allowed on the school premises. Immediate reporting: Promptly report any suspected abuse, misconduct, violation of school rules or activity that may put a child or any member of the school community at risk to the Executive Director for appropriate action. The Head of Security must perform these duties with integrity, fairness, discipline and respect for the dignity and rights of every child.",
