    "description": "Title of Post: Junior BIM & CAD Engineer Number of Post(s): 2 Founded in 2007 G.C with headquarters in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, by Swiss and Ethiopian partners, AEE intended from the outset to provide specialized structural engineering services not only in Ethiopia, but Africa, including prospective African markets, and to clients in Switzerland and other Western nations. AEE has the vision of becoming a team renowned for creating sustainable structures and relationships to satisfy clients, team and society. The values of AEE are: Pursue Excellence Be Proactive Integrate Holistically Prioritize Service Think and Do Creative Innovate Value Commit to Ethics Currently, AEE is scaling up its operations to meet growing customer demand and to continue to grow it in an innovative manner by so ensuring the continued satisfaction of our clientele. It is in this context and in an effort to ensure sustained growth that this vacancy is announced. As our vision, by 2035, we aspire to excel in sustainable structures and relationships satisfying both local and global clients, our team, and society. We are seeking a proactive and enthusiastic Junior BIM/ CAD Engineer to join our team on a full-time basis. This role involves production of structural construction documentation from concept to detail execution phase using different tools including BIM, CAD, spreadsheet, document processing and other relevant tools. Moreover, the tasks may include construction design, inspection, and management. For details regarding AEE, please refer to our web site www.aee.com.et . Position Type : The position shall involve successive stages from entry to full-time transition based on merit, as follows: BIM Trainee: 1 month of stipend paid training on location. On-the-job trainee: 2 months of increased stipend paid on-the-job training. Internship: 4 months internship with market competitive payment. Progression from one stage to the next shall be based on pertinent assessment. Job Summary: As a Junior BIM/CAD Engineer, your responsibilities will include: Efficient production of construction documentations in appropriate format (drawings, take-off/ Bill of quantity, cost estimate, specifications and etc.) with due consideration of quality and client requirements. Working on different materials (concrete, steel, timber, masonry) and construction practice (local, European and US). Eventual involvement in construction inspections, supervision and management. Duties + Responsibilities: Working closely with project leaders for accomplishment of project objectives which would include: Implementation of BIM & CAD in close collaboration with responsible company and/or project manager Construction detailing and drawings of structural works with due consideration of relevant concepts, codes and geographically customized practice. Other considerations would include construction sequence, relevant construction methods, and construction products. Supporting structural design team through BIM and CAD development and construction detailing Calculating structural bill of quantities, possibly using appropriate software and tools, and preparing specifications May include construction inspection, taking measurements on-site as deemed required and intermittent and/or resident supervision.",
